public static int longestPlateau(int[] a) {
    int best = 0;
    int run = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {
        if (i > 0 && a[i] == a[i - 1]) {
            run++;
        } else {
            run = 1;
        }
        if (run > best) {
            best = run;
        }
    }
    return best;
}

public static void shiftZerosToEnd(int[] a) {
    int next = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {
        if (a[i] != 0) {
            a[next] = a[i];
            next++;
        }
    }
    while (next < a.length) {
        a[next] = 0;
        next++;
    }
}
```
In `shiftZerosToEnd`, `next` is never ahead of `i`, so copying `a[i]` to `a[next]` cannot overwrite a nonzero value that has not been read yet.
